# Mini Online Shop: a slim request flow for the VS Code "REST Client" extension
# (JetBrains HTTP Client reads the same file). Start the stack first: docker compose up --build
# Run the requests top to bottom; later ones reuse values from earlier responses.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@email = demo@shop.test
@password = DemoShop123!

### 1. Log in as the seeded user (returns a JWT valid for 60 minutes)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2. Products: paged and sorted (public; no token needed). Highest price first, 5 per page.
# @name products
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?page=1&pageSize=5&sortBy=price&sortDirection=desc

### 3. Create an order with the coupon SAVE5 (first two products of the page above)
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{products.response.body.$.items[0].id}}", "quantity": 2 },
    { "productId": "{{products.response.body.$.items[1].id}}", "quantity": 1 }
  ],
  "couponCode": "SAVE5"
}

### 4. Read it back: server prices, snapshot coupon, subtotal / discount / total
# @name fetched
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 5. Replace it (whole state): new quantity, one line dropped, coupon removed with an explicit null
# @name updated
PUT {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{products.response.body.$.items[0].id}}", "quantity": 3 }
  ],
  "couponCode": null
}

### 6. Delete it (204 No Content)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 7. It is gone: 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 8. A failure: quantity 0 is rejected with 400 and a field error (items[0].quantity)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{products.response.body.$.items[0].id}}", "quantity": 0 }
  ],
  "couponCode": null
}
